    <item>
      <title>NIOSH graphene workplace exposure measurements</title>
      <link>https://graphenefacts.org/topics/policy/2026-09-16-niosh-graphene-exposure/</link>
      <pubDate>Wed, 16 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>https://graphenefacts.org/topics/policy/2026-09-16-niosh-graphene-exposure/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Evidence:&lt;/strong&gt; Well-supported occupational data; 10 µg/m³ is a band, not an OSHA PEL&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;NIOSH sampled workers at 11 US graphene producers/users. Many samples exceeded a conservative occupational exposure band of &lt;strong&gt;10 µg/m³&lt;/strong&gt; when dry powder was handled. Recommendation: supply graphene in masterbatch/liquid rather than loose powder. No reported human disease cluster tied to these data.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;See [[recurrence/log]] and [[weekly/2026-W38]].&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Archive file: &lt;a href=&#34;https://github.com/GrapheneFacts/graphene-archive/blob/main/topics/policy/2026-09-16-niosh-graphene-exposure.md&#34;&gt;topics/policy/2026-09-16-niosh-graphene-exposure.md&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>UCLA graphene stencil for molecular patterning</title>
      <link>https://graphenefacts.org/topics/engineering/2026-09-15-ucla-graphene-stencil/</link>
      <pubDate>Tue, 15 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>https://graphenefacts.org/topics/engineering/2026-09-15-ucla-graphene-stencil/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Evidence:&lt;/strong&gt; Well-supported (2015 paper). &lt;strong&gt;2026 appearance:&lt;/strong&gt; Recurrence.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Full write-up: [[posts/holey-graphene-molecular-stencil]]&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Graphene mask with holes on gold places molecules only where intended. Landmark: Thomas et al., &lt;em&gt;ACS Nano&lt;/em&gt; 2015, DOI 10.1021/acsnano.5b03936. UCLA Health reran the institutional story on 14–15 Sep 2026.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Source:&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;a href=&#34;https://www.uclahealth.org/news/release/ucla-scientists-create-graphene-barrier-to-precisely-control-molecules-for-making-nanoelectronics&#34;&gt;UCLA Health&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Week context: [[weekly/2026-W38]] · [[recurrence/log]]&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
